      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the workaround which the lab said would work and which BoringSSL uses for its FIPS certification.  It sounded like it is important for there to be a function inside the \"FIPS module\" which is called from outside the \"FIPS module\" to supply it with entropy, which is the inverse of the expected order.  That requires the global buffer to queue the entropy up in.  I\u0027ll check with them whether a simpler solution would also work, where the \"FIPS module\" calls something like \"select_entropy_source()\" outside the module which returns a pointer to get_random_bytes (but which we could say could be changed to return something else).  Remember this is FIPS certification though, so it doesn\u0027t have to make sense :-(",
      "parentUuid": "590f4c1c_8dc8c80b",
      "revId": "7783b95ceef72ab9ddcef5dc20751648a9ba0acc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
